{
  "info": {
    "name": "TechTrax MCP",
    "description": "Manual testing for the TechTrax MCP server (Streamable HTTP, stateful).\n\nFlow: run the requests top to bottom.\n1. `initialize` captures the `Mcp-Session-Id` header into the `sessionId` collection variable (see its Tests tab).\n2. `notifications/initialized` completes the handshake.\n3. `tools/list` shows the catalog — confirm every tool now has a `tenantId` param.\n4. `tools/call` requests pass `tenantId` in `arguments`.\n\n⚠️ Authorization / `x-actor-role`: this server reads request headers ONCE, on `initialize`. The `x-actor-role` header therefore belongs on the `initialize` request only (it is set there via the `actorRole` variable) and applies to the whole session — putting it on a `tools/call` has no effect. `actorRole` defaults to `receptionist` so the staff + CRM tools show up. Set it to `patient` (least privilege) and re-run `initialize` to see the CRM/statistics/patient tools disappear from `tools/list` and get rejected on call. A session = one actor; to switch role, re-run `initialize`.\n\nEdit collection variables (baseUrl, tenantId, apiKey, actorRole, leadId, assigneeId) under the collection's Variables tab.\n\nNote: responses come back as SSE (`text/event-stream`) by default. The body shows a `data: {...}` line. To get plain JSON instead, set `enableJsonResponse: true` in `src/app.module.ts` (dev only).\n\nSee docs/MANUAL_TESTING.md and docs/MCP_TOOL_AUTHORIZATION.md for the full guide.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3100",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tenantId",
      "value": "6650f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "actorRole",
      "value": "receptionist",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "leadId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "assigneeId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. initialize",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Capture the MCP session id so later requests can reuse the session.",
              "const sid = pm.response.headers.get('mcp-session-id');",
              "if (sid) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', sid);",
              "  console.log('Captured Mcp-Session-Id:', sid);",
              "} else {",
              "  console.warn('No Mcp-Session-Id header on the initialize response.');",
              "}",
              "pm.test('initialize returned a session id', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(sid, 'Mcp-Session-Id header').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}", "description": "Only needed if MCP_CLIENT_API_KEY is set on the server. Leave apiKey empty in dev." },
          { "key": "x-actor-role", "value": "{{actorRole}}", "description": "Who the AI acts as: patient | doctor | receptionist | admin. MUST be set here on initialize — the server reads it once per session. Defaults to receptionist so staff + CRM tools appear. Set actorRole=patient to test least-privilege." }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": { \"name\": \"postman\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\" }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Opens an MCP session. The response is SSE; the important part is the `Mcp-Session-Id` response header, captured automatically by the Tests script.\n\nThe `x-actor-role` header set here (from the `actorRole` variable) scopes the ENTIRE session's authorization — it is read once, at init, and cannot be changed per call. Re-run this request after changing `actorRole` to switch actor."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "2. notifications/initialized",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"method\": \"notifications/initialized\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Completes the MCP handshake. Expect 202 Accepted with an empty body."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "3. tools/list",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 2,\n  \"method\": \"tools/list\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Lists all tools. Confirm each tool's inputSchema.properties now includes a `tenantId` field (24-char hex)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4a. tools/call - list_doctors (happy path)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 3,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"tenant_info.list_doctors\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"specialty\": \"cardiology\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Passes tenantId as a tool argument. With a valid 24-hex tenantId and the backend up, returns real doctor data."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4b. tools/call - get_clinic_profile",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 4,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"tenant_info.get_clinic_profile\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"format\": \"markdown\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Clinic profile in markdown format."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4c. tools/call - appointment_summary",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 5,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"statistics.get_appointment_summary\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"from\": \"2026-07-01\",\n      \"to\": \"2026-07-07\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Statistics tool with tenantId + date range in arguments. Staff-only (statistics:read) — appears/runs only when actorRole is doctor/receptionist/admin."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4d. tools/call - crm.list_teams (step 1 of lead assignment)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 9,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"crm.list_teams\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"format\": \"markdown\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "CRM (lead:read, staff-only). Lists teams with name + description so the AI can pick the right team for a lead. Copy a team `id` from the result into the `crm.get_team` call. Requires actorRole = receptionist/doctor/admin (a patient session won't see this tool)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4e. tools/call - crm.get_team (step 2: members)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 10,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"crm.get_team\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"teamId\": \"PUT_A_TEAM_ID_HERE\",\n      \"format\": \"markdown\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "CRM (lead:read, staff-only). Returns the team's teamLead + members (id, name, role). Pick the owner's id (teamLead._id or a members[]._id) to use as `assignedTo` in crm.assign_lead. Replace PUT_A_TEAM_ID_HERE with an id from crm.list_teams."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4f. tools/call - crm.assign_lead (method 1: specific member)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 11,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"crm.assign_lead\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"leadId\": \"{{leadId}}\",\n      \"assignedTo\": \"{{assigneeId}}\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "CRM (lead:write, staff-only) — WRITE. Method 1 of 3: reassign an EXISTING lead (leadId) to a SPECIFIC user (assignedTo, from crm.get_team). Backend rejects an assignee who isn't an active, non-admin member. Set the `leadId` and `assigneeId` collection variables first. Re-owns the lead + notifies — run against a scratch tenant."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4g. tools/call - crm.assign_lead (method 2: team lead)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 12,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"crm.assign_lead\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"leadId\": \"{{leadId}}\",\n      \"teamId\": \"PUT_A_TEAM_ID_HERE\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "CRM (lead:write) — WRITE. Method 2 of 3: pass `teamId` only (no assignedTo, no isRoundRobin) → the lead goes to that team's designated team lead. Replace PUT_A_TEAM_ID_HERE with an id from crm.list_teams."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4h. tools/call - crm.assign_lead (method 3: round-robin)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 13,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"crm.assign_lead\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"{{tenantId}}\",\n      \"leadId\": \"{{leadId}}\",\n      \"teamId\": \"PUT_A_TEAM_ID_HERE\",\n      \"isRoundRobin\": true\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "CRM (lead:write) — WRITE. Method 3 of 3: `teamId` + `isRoundRobin:true` → auto-distribute across the team's MEMBERS (team lead excluded), load-aware (fewest open leads first). No specific person needed. `assignedTo` + `isRoundRobin` together is rejected. Replace PUT_A_TEAM_ID_HERE with an id from crm.list_teams."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "5a. Negative - missing tenant",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 6,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"tenant_info.list_doctors\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "No tenantId argument and no x-tenant-id header. Expect isError:true with 'Tenant context is missing...'."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "5b. Negative - malformed tenant",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 7,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"tenant_info.list_doctors\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"tenantId\": \"abc\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Malformed tenantId. Expect a JSON-RPC validation error: 'tenantId must be a 24-character hex id (MongoDB ObjectId)'."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Legacy - tenant via x-tenant-id header",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" },
          { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{apiKey}}" },
          { "key": "Mcp-Session-Id", "value": "{{sessionId}}" },
          { "key": "x-tenant-id", "value": "{{tenantId}}" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 8,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"tenant_info.list_doctors\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mcp"] },
        "description": "Backward-compat check: no tenantId argument, tenant supplied via the x-tenant-id header instead. Should still resolve and return data."
      }
    }
  ]
}
